Return JSON with two arrays:
- "background": what NOTES add that CURRENT doesn't already say, one line per section below, in this order, each written as "<label>：<facts>" with the label exactly as given. Put several facts in one line separated by "；". Leave out a section when NOTES add nothing to it. Never contradict CURRENT. Only what helps in meetings; no line over 120 characters.
  Sections: "身分", "公司", "用 Parley 做什麼", "負責的工作", "常開的會議", "常見講者", "溝通偏好".
- "terms": at most 6 proper nouns particular to this user that a speech recogniser would likely get wrong: their company's name, their products', and their customers' or partners' company names. Leave out everyday words, job or tech jargon, acronyms, command and file names, and well-known tools and services (GitHub, Discord, Slack, Google…). Fewer is better; an empty list is fine. Exactly as written, one name per entry, no descriptions.
Skip coding conventions, tool configuration, file paths, secrets, credentials and anything about other people's private lives.


Return your answer strictly as a single JSON object matching the provided schema. Use the schema's property names EXACTLY (verbatim) — do not rename, translate, or add top-level keys.

